Jenkins Shared Libraries — a way to reuse pipeline code across multiple projects.

🔹 Instead of writing repetitive steps in every Jenkinsfile, you can store common logic in a shared library.
🔹 This makes pipelines more scalable, maintainable, and standardized across teams.
🔹 Example: one shared function for code checkout, testing, or notifications can be used by all projects.

Key takeaway: Shared Libraries = Clean, DRY (Don’t Repeat Yourself), and professional pipelines.
